```
On POSIX, writes to a *pipe* stderr are asynchronous; `process.exit` does not flush pending writes. Every other failure path in the CLI sets `process.exitCode` and returns (see `outputError` in `packages/cli/src/output/formatter.ts:68`), which lets the event loop drain. `wafflebase login 2>&1 | tee log` can therefore lose the one prose line that explains the failure.
